meta {
  name: Update Product (PATCH)
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

patch {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "label": "New Label",
    "status": "Completed"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.label: isString
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against a disposable scratch product
  (`WC-TEST-PATCH-001`, id `6aa98167a30ca5945169a245`, created and deleted
  in this same test run) on "David's Dev Account". `openapi_pimv3.json`
  now formally declares `PATCH /products/{identifier}` (it did not before
  this spec refresh) -- this was already empirically confirmed working in
  Phase 2 (quirks #26/#27 in `config/api-testing.config.md`), but never
  had its own dedicated `.bru` file until now.

  ## What it does
  Partial update of a product. Any subset of `ProductUpdateInputDto`
  fields may be sent; unset fields are left untouched. Returns `200` with
  the **full** updated product (all fields, not just the ones patched) --
  matches `openapi_pimv3.json`'s declared `200`, contradicts `API V3.md`'s
  stated 204-for-PATCH convention (also flagged project-wide in quirk
  #56).

  ## Key fields confirmed in this run
  - `label` and `status` both apply immediately and round-trip in the
    response.
  - The response shape here is richer than `POST`'s create-response
    (adds `assets`, `categories`, `relationships` arrays, `created_user_audit`/
    `modified_user_audit`, `product_type`) -- same shape as a plain `GET`.

  ## ⚠️ TWO CORRECTIONS, 2026-10-08
  **(a) This endpoint returns `204`, not `200`.** The "What it does" section
  above still describes the 2026-09-15 behavior. `PATCH` switched to `204 No
  Content` with an empty body somewhere between 2026-09-23 and 2026-10-01
  (quirk #84) and was re-confirmed `204` on 2026-10-08. There is no response
  body to read; verify with a follow-up `GET`.

  **(b) Every `*_ids` field is now REJECTED on `PATCH`.** `category_ids`,
  `static_list_ids`, `channel_ids`, `ecatalog_ids` and
  `product_data_sheet_ids` each return `422 {"errors":[{"name":
  "InputDTOValidationError","description":"<field>: Extra inputs are not
  permitted"}]}`, although `ProductUpdateInputDto` still declares all five
  (quirk #93). Confirmed still accepted: `label`, `gtin`, `status`,
  `attributes`, `thumbnail_id`, `product_family_id`, `parent_id`. Category
  linking moved to `POST /products/{id}/categories` and
  `DELETE /products/{id}/categories/{category_id}` -- see
  `Link Category to Product.bru` and `Unlink Category from Product.bru`.

  Also confirmed 2026-10-08: `{"thumbnail_id": null}` clears the thumbnail
  (`204`, follow-up `GET` shows `thumbnail_id: null`) -- quirk #97.

  ## Related, resource-specific quirks (see config for the full list)
  - ~~`category_ids`/other relationship-array fields reliably apply via
    `PATCH` even when silently dropped on `POST` for some resources
    (quirk #27)~~ -- **retracted 2026-10-08, see correction (b) above.**
  - `DELETE /products/{id}/{path}` used to ignore `{path}` and delete the
    whole product (quirk #31) -- confirmed FIXED 2026-09-23, now safely
    rejects with `405`/`404` instead. See "Delete Product.bru" for the
    current behavior.

  ## ⚠️ Verify relationship-array fields via `_fields`, not the dedicated subpath
  As of 2026-09-23, `GET /products/{id}/categories`, `.../assets`, and
  `.../static_lists` are confirmed BROKEN -- they always return an empty
  array, even for a product with real, confirmed links. This makes those
  subpaths useless for verifying whether a `PATCH`'s `category_ids` /
  `static_list_ids` actually applied. Use
  `GET /products?_fields=categories&_fields=assets&_fields=static_lists&sku=...`
  instead -- confirmed correct. See "Get Product Subpath - Attributes.bru"
  for the full writeup; this bug is what caused this file's own
  2026-09-22 example to wrongly report `static_list_ids` as a no-op.
}

example {
  name: 200 - Success
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 against a disposable scratch product on "David's Dev Account".

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa98167a30ca5945169a245
    method: patch
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "label": "WC Test Patch Product Updated",
        "status": "Completed"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "assets": [],
            "attributes": {
              "amazon_ready": 0.0,
              "basic_information_completeness": 0.0,
              "english_content_completeness": 0.0,
              "google_shopping_completeness": 0.0,
              "marketing_ready": 0.0,
              "product_specifications_completeness": 0.0,
              "shopify_ready": 0.0,
              "spanish_content_completeness": 0.0,
              "website_ready": 7.14
            },
            "categories": [],
            "created": "2026-09-15T17:33:27.474000+00:00",
            "created_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "id": "6aa98167a30ca5945169a245",
            "label": "WC Test Patch Product Updated",
            "modified": "2026-09-15T17:33:38.480000+00:00",
            "modified_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "num_variations": 0,
            "overwritten_attributes": [],
            "product_family_id": null,
            "product_family_model_id": null,
            "product_level": 0,
            "product_type": "SINGLE",
            "relationships": [],
            "sku": "WC-TEST-PATCH-001",
            "status": "Completed"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 200 - Full Parameters
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-23 against a fresh disposable product/parent pair. All 8 fields that CAN succeed together on this account are sent in one PATCH: label, gtin, status, attributes, thumbnail_id, category_ids, static_list_ids, and parent_id -- and every one of them genuinely applies. CORRECTION to the 2026-09-22 version of this example: that version claimed static_list_ids silently no-ops -- this was a false positive caused by checking via the broken GET /products/{id}/static_lists subpath (see "Get Product Subpath - Attributes.bru" -- that subpath, and /categories and /assets, are confirmed broken as of 2026-09-23, always returning an empty array regardless of real linkage). Verified here via the CORRECT method instead: GET /products?_fields=static_lists&sku=... on the search endpoint, which shows the list membership genuinely applied. NOT included: product_family_id -- sending it together with parent_id in the same PATCH returns 422 "product data validation failed" (see the dedicated 422 example below; this mirrors the identical conflict already documented on POST /products in "Create Product - Full Featured.bru"). NOT included: channel_ids, ecatalog_ids, product_data_sheet_ids -- all three are gated behind the same UEF feature flag; see the 403 example below, which also documents that including ANY of these three fields blocks the ENTIRE PATCH, not just those fields (confirmed by sending all 12 ProductUpdateInputDto fields together and getting a 403 with none of the other 9 fields applied).

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6ab41416ebb26b08b2285eea
    method: patch
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "label": "WC Test Subpaths Product Updated",
        "gtin": "01234567890128",
        "status": "Completed",
        "attributes": {"wc_test_text": "WC max-params patch value"},
        "thumbnail_id": "6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f",
        "category_ids": ["6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc", "6a9f1b542b6fd055ffb7c7dd"],
        "static_list_ids": ["6aa025bd2b6fd055ffb7cab4"],
        "parent_id": "6ab41478ebb26b08b2285eeb"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "_parent_id": "6ab41478ebb26b08b2285eeb",
            "assets": [
              {
                "id": "6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f",
                "filename": "wc_test_asset_renamed.jpg",
                "file_size": 17726,
                "thumbnail": "https://files.dev.plytix.com/.../wc_test_asset_renamed.jpg",
                "url": "https://files.dev.plytix.com/.../wc_test_asset_renamed.jpg"
              }
            ],
            "attributes": {
              "amazon_ready": 0.0,
              "basic_information_completeness": 0.0,
              "english_content_completeness": 0.0,
              "google_shopping_completeness": 0.0,
              "marketing_ready": 0.0,
              "product_specifications_completeness": 0.0,
              "shopify_ready": 0.0,
              "spanish_content_completeness": 0.0,
              "wc_test_text": "WC max-params patch value",
              "website_ready": 21.43
            },
            "categories": [
              {"id": "6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc", "name": "WC Test Category", "path": ["WC Test Category"]},
              {"id": "6a9f1b542b6fd055ffb7c7dd", "name": "WC Test Child Category", "path": ["WC Test Category", "WC Test Child Category"]}
            ],
            "created": "2026-09-23T18:01:57.966000+00:00",
            "created_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "gtin": "01234567890128",
            "id": "6ab41416ebb26b08b2285eea",
            "label": "WC Test Subpaths Product Updated",
            "modified": "2026-09-23T18:03:46.483000+00:00",
            "modified_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "num_variations": 0,
            "overwritten_attributes": [],
            "product_family_id": null,
            "product_family_model_id": null,
            "product_level": 2,
            "product_type": "VARIANT",
            "relationships": [],
            "sku": "WC-TEST-SUBPATHS-001",
            "status": "Completed",
            "thumbnail": {
              "id": "6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f",
              "filename": "wc_test_asset_renamed.jpg",
              "file_size": 17726,
              "thumbnail": "https://files.dev.plytix.com/.../wc_test_asset_renamed.jpg",
              "url": "https://files.dev.plytix.com/.../wc_test_asset_renamed.jpg"
            },
